# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. Both are read at BUILD time,
# so a running dev server has to be restarted after a change.
#
# There is no secret here by design: the anon key is meant to be shipped to
# every visitor, and row-level security — not secrecy — is what keeps one
# user's garage out of another's browser (SHR-01). If the value you are about
# to paste is labelled `service_role` or starts with `sb_secret_`, it is the
# wrong one and the build will refuse it.
#
# Where to find them: Supabase dashboard → Settings → API keys. Full runbook in
# specs/002-montero-garage/HANDOFF-T2-202-SUPABASE.md.
#
# Both may be left unset: the site builds, every check passes, and the sign-in
# page says accounts are not switched on yet.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
